Current Version can be found [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Endogeny here].
[[File:Endogeny (Beta 16.0 - Beta 41.0)|thumb|220x220px|Beta 16.0 - Beta 41.0]]
Endogeny used to cost 7G and had the stats of 4/4. '''Beta 1.6''' buffed it to 5/5, but '''Beta 4.8''' returned it to 4/4. '''Beta 5.0''' gave it only +1 ATK this time, but also increased the cost to 8G. '''Beta 7.2''' returned that to 7G, though, while '''Beta 16.0''' gave it -1 ATK, returning it to its original version yet again.
[[File:Endogeny (Beta 41.1).png|thumb|294x294px|Beta 41.1]]
'''Beta 19.0''' brought its cost back up to 8, but kept it at 4/4. '''Beta 33.0''' added Tribe icons, but it came at the cost of Endogeny's [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Dog Dog] Tribe, making it now only part of the [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Amalgamate Amalgamate] one. '''Beta 36.1''' nerfed it further, this time by its first effect change. It will now reduce the cost of the returned card by 2. '''Beta 41.1''' allowed multiple tribes to function again, giving back its Dog Tribe.
[[File:Endogeny (Beta 46.0).png|thumb|291x291px|Beta 46.0]]
'''Beta 46.0''' reworked it entirely. It now makes use of the new Synergy effect, giving +1/+1 to all Amalgamates and Dogs in your hand when played if you've played another of either Tribe beforehand in the same turn. It also gained +1 ATK, bringing it back up to 5, while its cost dropped by 3G. This gives it its lowest cost so far, being at 5 as well.

This didn't last long, as '''Beta 51.0''' reverted it back almost entirely with its ATK returning to 4, but its cost increasing to a new hight of 9G. Its Magic is now targetable, but it doesn't reduce the target's cost, making the Magic function exactly like [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Expulsion Expulsion].
